{"name":"Baked Sienna","hex":"#9b775e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baked","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of bake"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That has been cooked by baking.","Inebriated: drunk, high, or stoned."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baked"},{"term":"sienna","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A form of clay containing iron and manganese.","A pigment with a reddish-brown colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["having a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sienna"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baking","blocks":[{"text":"Baking is a method of preparing food that uses dry heat, typically in an oven, hot ashes, or on hot stones. The most commonly baked foods in 2025 were bread and rolls. Heat is gradually transferred from the surface of unbaked goods to their center, typically at elevated temperatures surpassing 300 °F. Dry heat cooking imparts a distinctive richness to foods through the processes of caramelization and surface browning. As heat travels through, it transforms batters and doughs into baked goods and more with a firm dry crust and a softer center. Baking can be combined with grilling to produce a hybrid barbecue variant by using both methods simultaneously, or one after the other. Baking is related to barbecuing because the concept of the masonry oven is similar to that of a smoke pit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg/330px-Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baking"},{"title":"Sienna","blocks":[{"text":"Sienna is an earth pigment containing iron oxide and manganese oxide. In its natural state, it is yellowish brown, and it is called raw sienna. When heated, it becomes a reddish brown, and it is called burnt sienna. It takes its name from the city-state of Siena, where it was produced during the Renaissance. Along with ochre and umber, it was one of the first pigments to be used by humans, and is found in many cave paintings. Since the Renaissance, it has been one of the brown pigments most widely used by artists."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sienna"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg/500px-Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg/1280px-Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg/500px-Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lasagna that has been baked","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARao's_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Anders_Zorn_-_Br%C3%B6dbaket.jpg/500px-Anders_Zorn_-_Br%C3%B6dbaket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Anders_Zorn_-_Br%C3%B6dbaket.jpg/1280px-Anders_Zorn_-_Br%C3%B6dbaket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Anders_Zorn_-_Br%C3%B6dbaket.jpg/500px-Anders_Zorn_-_Br%C3%B6dbaket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anders Zorn – B